{
 "about": "Each species walks a fixed course (d172's courses); only the animal on the course is tracked. Its contacts are measured on the skinned mesh itself (the foot bone and its children, skinned on the CPU every frame): a run of frames with the sole on the sand and still; for the gerbil each landing (the sole's lowest skin back within 5 mm of the sand after lifting 9 mm clear), placed where it first touches. Each print is matched to the nearest contact whose run covers the print's time ±0.25 s; a print with none within 10 cm has no matching contact. Offsets in cm.",
